  "launcher": {
    "comment": "The RPG-7 (the game designer's launcher pack /Game/Launcher_Animations, 2026-11-09; the pack is the user's - never modified, read here by path): body \"full\" (the designer 2026-11-09 b: the pack's legs too - flip to \"upper\" for the torso only on the ABP's legs): every bone but the root from the pack, the in-place loops played at speed / their authored speed per direction (walk_speeds / jog_speeds / crouch_speeds / sprint_speed = the planted ball-of-the-foot speed of the MALE retargeted copies, measured at 240 Hz - the pack's *_Root variants' root travel does not match their feet, e.g. Walk_Right 150 cm/s of root travel vs 77 of planted foot; the *_Root clips are not used, the capsule moves the body; crouch_body upper: crouched, only the torso is the pack's - its crouch walk shuffles the feet (they slid 76 % of the speed, RpgAnimSmoke), the legs are the ABP's crouch; root_translation reference: the root is the reference pose's - translation too: on the ABP's lowered crouch root the pack's crouch feet sank ~8 cm), max_play_rate 2.4 so the sprint keeps its feet; phase_offsets = each loop's left heel strike (the left ball's farthest point along the travel, as a share of the loop, measured on the male copies at 240 Hz: the pack's loops are NOT phase-aligned - forward / right 0, back / left ~0.5, run right 0.125, run left 0.38), so a direction blend plants the same foot; stride_scale = the female copies' feet against the male (x0.945, measured); walk -> run over jog_blend_speeds 140 -> 180 (his 220 cm/s = the run loops at ~x1.2); the shot / reload take the torso only, the legs keep walking. Set_02 = the launcher on the shoulder (idle, walk / run 4 directions, crouch idle + crouch walk 4 directions, the shot, the reload, the aim-offset poses, hits, deaths); Set_01 = a lowered carry: only its Run_Fast is used (the sprint, nobody sprints with the tube shouldered). The squad's UE4 skeletons play IK-retargeted copies (retargeted; Scripts/Editor/setup_launcher_animation.py, the same UE4 rig both ways). pack_playback false: a skeleton with no copies gets no launcher layer at all (the PMC operator HAS copies since 2026-11-09, feat/rpg-ai-pmc: /Game/Characters/Animations/Launcher/Pmc, IK-retargeted UE4 -> UE5 onto SKM_PmcOperator by the same script) (the pack is a UE4 mannequin: by bone name it would bend a UE5 body). fire_* play natively on the upper body (the kick starts on frame 0, measured: the rocket leaves at the trigger, no delay); reload_* fit the weapon's reload_time after the shot's follow-through (reload_insert_s = the clip time the left hand pushes the rocket onto the tube - the rocket on the model shows from there; measured by setup_launcher_animation.py); aim_poses = the last frame of the Rotation_90_* clips against their first (the shouldered idle), mesh-space additives on a 3 x 3 grid at aim_yaw_range_deg / aim_pitch_range_deg (measured: left -91.5 / right +88.8 deg yaw, up +85.8 / down -89 deg pitch); the corners are the sums of the edges - the pack's Rotation_45_* poses (aim_poses_diagonals: retargeted, NOT used) were measured off the grid's corners (up-left -74 / +35, up-right +58 / +33, down-left -95 / -55, down-right +89 / -50 deg), so they would aim wrong there; hits = the upper-body hit reaction, deaths = the standing death (front hit -> deaths[0] falls backwards, from behind -> deaths[1] falls forwards). turn_* = turn in place standing still: the clips turn 90 deg in their root (dropped), so their time follows the body's own yaw (the feet stay planted).",
